<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.3.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01784</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.3.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f524df07-7b2c-4689-8cf0-9d386177b611</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <exercise id="a86be7e9-a521-420f-bc87-0699ce61b7bf" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">Sketch or describe the figure in Step 4 and Step 15. 
              <media alt="Three steps of a growing pattern">
                <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_05_10_01.jpg"/>
              </media>
           </para>
          <para id="para-00003">How many small squares are in Step 4?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00004">Correct! Step 4 is a 4-by-4 array of squares with the lower-left corner square moved to the upper-right corner.</para>
          <para id="para-00005">Try again. Revisit activities 7.3.2 and 7.3.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00006">The correct answer is 16.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_1efcfb52-3163-409c-870a-e78eba258ba3" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00007">How many small squares are in Step 15?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00008">Correct! Step 15 is a 15-by-15 array of squares with the lower-left corner square moved to the upper-right corner.</para>
          <para id="para-00009">Try again. Revisit activities 7.3.2 and 7.3.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00010">The correct answer is 225.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="bae33e1e-93fa-45e0-80cf-05879f2e5c72" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00011">Which equation represents the relationship between the step number, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, and the number of small squares, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, in each step?</para>
          <para id="para-00012">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00013"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00014"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00015"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00016"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00017">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00018">Try again. Revisit activities 7.3.2 and 7.3.3.</para>
          <para id="para-00019">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_75564220-9969-4f6b-8201-1514dbe3b2c4" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00020">Each figure is composed of large squares and small squares. The side length of the large square is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>. Choose the correct expression that represents the area, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, of the shaded part of each figure.</para>
          <para id="para-00021">Figure A 
              <media alt="Large square with 1 by 1 small squares removed from each corner.">
                <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_05_10_02.svg"/>
              </media>
           </para>
          <para id="para-00022">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00023"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00024"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00025"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00026"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00027">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> The figure is an <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-by-<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> square with 4 unit squares that aren’t shaded.</para>
          <para id="para-00028">Try again. Revisit activity 7.3.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00029">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. The figure is an <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-by-<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> square with 4 unit squares that aren’t shaded.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="f4885315-c632-49bd-8ced-821d528863a3" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00030">Figure B 
              <media alt="2 large squares side by side. On the side of the right square, there are 2 small squares stacked vertically, each with dimensions 2 by 2.">
                <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_05_10_03.svg"/>
              </media>
           </para>
          <para id="para-00031">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00032"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00033"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00034"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00035"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00036">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. There are two squares that are <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, and there are smaller squares that are 4 units each added to the figure.</para>
          <para id="para-00037">Try again. Revisit activities 7.3.2.</para>
          <para id="para-00038">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. There are two squares that are <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, and there are smaller squares that are 4 units each added to the figure.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_00953db5-9afb-4be6-92c1-ef559312ee4d" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00039">Use the sequence below to answer questions a and b.</para>
          <para id="para-00040">How many squares are in Step 5?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00041">Correct! Every step has one more row and column than the step number, and then one square is taken away.</para>
          <para id="para-00042">Try again. Revisit activities 7.3.3 and 7.3.4.</para>
          <para id="para-00043">The correct answer is 35.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_5fe140cf-4801-41b8-a65b-577282d9e5db" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00044">Choose the correct expression that represents the area, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, of the shaded part of each figure for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> steps.</para>
          <para id="para-00045">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00046"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00047"><m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00048"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00049"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00050">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00051">Try again. Revisit activities 7.3.3 and 7.3.4.</para>
          <para id="para-00052">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>n</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>